+# DEV run C4-S1 — failure analysis (cycle 2, contract §10 C9 "popular rival")
+
+Run dirs (read-only, `mode=ro`): `scratchpad/runs/C4-S1` (system, run `run_9cf7a316a832`, code `54fec3f`, 103/120 = 0.858) and
+`scratchpad/runs/C4-S1-baseline-source` (116/120). Per class, system: cross_domain 28/40, fault 5/10, every other class
+perfect (coincidence 10, copies 7, common_origin_pos 8, contradiction 10, temporal 10, single_domain 10, denied 10, cross_tenant 5).
+Baseline fails dev-018, dev-039, dev-102, dev-104 (none of them a system failure). All 17 system failures are **abstains** on
+positives (`extracted=abstain`, `reason=wrong_option`); no leak, no tie, no error.
+
+Everything below was read from `coord.db` (`question.route` audit, `claims`, `conflicts`, `responses`, `questions`), the
+holder `evidence.db`s, the asker views and the dev gold. Scripts: `scratchpad/analyze_c4.py` (per-task dump, adapted from
+`analyze_s1.py`) and `scratchpad/summ_c4.py` (one block per task; the tables below are its output).
+
+## 0. Headline
+
+The S1 problems are gone: routing by term index reaches the gold holders (16/17 failed tasks had **every** gold holder
+routed, dev-017 had 2/3 in two departments), the evaluator keeps the gold and the rival statements in **separate** clusters
+(one claim per service — never merged), and the gate does exactly what the contract wants: the gold claim is `supported`
+(3–4 independent roots, 2 departments) and the rival claim is `hypothesis` ("independent roots span 1 department unit(s);
+the question requires 2").
+
+All 17 failures diverge at the same, new place, **(e) conflict handling**: `evaluate_responses` reports the gold statement and
+the rival statement as a *disagreement* ("Numbers differ: 19 vs 50" — they share ≥3 content tokens: the context phrase
+`ivory jetty` plus the boilerplate token `service`), the engine turns that pair into a conflict between the two committed
+claims, and `_open_conflict_sync` sets **both** claims to `contested` regardless of their gate status. The contradiction
+follow-up is then routed *away* from the holders behind both sides (`already_supports` penalty), reaches 0 gold holders in
+16/17 cases, finds "0 support A, 0 support B, records still disagree: True" and leaves the conflict `investigating`. The
+asker view ends with two `contested` claims; extraction reads only `supported` claims → abstain.
+
+The split is exact: a positive **passes iff the rival department is not one of the question's two departments** (23/23
+passing question tasks: rival not routable → 0 rival answers → 0 conflicts; 17/17 failing: rival in a question department
+→ R rival answers → 1 conflict). R (2–7 in this seed) does not matter: R=2 fails as surely as R=7.
+
+The baseline passes the same 17 tasks because its commit path is asymmetric by accident: findings are gated with
+`has_open_conflict=False` (gold finding → `supported`, rival finding → `hypothesis` by the department rule) and the
+disagreement *sides* are committed as separate 1-root `contested` claims next to them (dev-025: 2 findings + 30 contested side
+claims). The supported gold finding survives and extraction picks it.
+
+Run-wide, **1241 of the 1690 conflicts** opened in this run are between two claims that each name exactly one service and
+name *different* services — 73% of all conflict investigations (and their loop budget) were spent on "A says X is the cause,
+B says Y is the cause", which is competing evidence, not a contradiction of a record.
+
